# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PART 1: CORE BEHAVIOR & STABILIZATION DIRECTIVES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## 1. Think Before Coding
* Never guess data schemas, API contract structures, or transatlantic policy text.
* If a data pipeline or regional ingestion flow is ambiguous, ask clarifying questions before proposing a fix.
* Analyze existing database models, Typescript types, and constraints fully before touching code.

## 2. Simplicity First
* Write the absolute minimum code necessary to resolve data or UI inconsistencies.
* Strictly enforce a zero over-engineering policy. 
* Use Tailwind CSS utility classes directly for UI fixes. Do not add custom raw CSS selectors unless entirely necessary.

## 3. Hyper-Surgical Changes
* You are in a critical stabilization window. Target only the exact lines causing data loss, incorrect formatting, or visual layout bugs.
* Do NOT rewrite adjacent code, reformat untouched functions, or perform passive "clean-ups."
* Fewer lines of code changed is always the superior solution. Minimize the blast radius of every commit.

## 4. Goal-Driven Execution & Verification
* Isolate, fix, and verify each bug sequentially. 
* Every numeric rendering change must be checked programmatically or logically across all active markets before completion.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PART 2: POST-STABILIZATION PLATFORM AUDIT DIRECTIVES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IMMEDIATELY following successful file updates, verification on localhost:3001, 
# and deployment to the Vercel staging site, Antigravity MUST execute a comprehensive 
# end-to-end Platform Audit.

## 1. Data Integrity & Ingestion Review
* Audit every regional data mapper and ingestion endpoint across all active global markets.
* Ensure no values are dropped, unmapped, or truncated incorrectly by the data ingestion backend.
* Cross-verify that all frontend dashboard statistics strictly mirror the underlying database schemas.

## 2. Global UI/UX & Tailwind Consistency Audit
* Manually click through and review every dashboard tab, form page, and data grid layout.
* Check layout components across both strict Light Mode and Dark Mode settings.
* Eliminate all instances of unreadable text, broken contrast ratios, element clipping, overlapping boundaries, and dead clickable nodes.
* Standardize layout margins, card roundedness, padding depths, and typographic hierarchies to ensure an uncompromised institutional user experience.

## 3. Audit Logging & Verification Export
* Generate a comprehensive, markdown-formatted Comprehensive Audit Report upon completion.
* Log all discovered design discrepancies, corrected elements, and verified operational statuses.
* Present the complete review report in this chat log file for final user sign-off.
